    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d212">

                <pb facs="0643" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg521"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Preston to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-02-04"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 4,
                        1889</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Steam-lighter <hi rendition="#italic">Admiral</hi>, at pier 10, North River, New
                    York, has on board armament of rebel steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Madrid</hi>, consisting of several one-hundred-pounder Parrot cannons with ship
                    carriages and several hundred projectiles, part received from William Reed &amp;
                    Son of Boston, and part from from Joseph Frazer, of New York. They are, we
                    believe, intended to be shipped on the tender of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Madrid</hi>, the American steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Carondelet</hi>,
                    now at Erie Basin, or on another vessel, for a neutral port, but in fact for
                    Cape Hayti. Collector Magone advised, asked to telegraph to you for immediate
                    instructions to act.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stephen Preston.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
